Sticker packs are stored and managed by the core now (core sticker packs
patch); this is the UI for them.

- Composer sticker tab: packs come from getStickerPacks (sorted by name,
  ids instead of paths) and deleting removes the pack entry via
  removeSticker instead of deleting the file, which is a blob shared with
  messages now. A "Manage Stickers" button sits under the packs.
- Empty sticker tab: "Find Sticker Packs" opens the Public Bots directory
  pre-searched for "sticker" (its consent step applies) with a
  community-run note, hidden with the other community suggestions (user
  setting or instance-wide); plus "Import Pack (.zip)" and "Manage".
- Manage Stickers dialog: new/rename/delete/export packs, drag stickers
  between packs (Ctrl/Alt copies) or use Move to / Copy to from the context
  menu (long press on touch), add image files, a "Recently Seen" strip of
  chat stickers that are in no pack yet, and packs of the user's other
  profiles to import.
- A received .zip that holds a sticker pack renders as a pack card (four
  stickers, name, count, "Add Sticker Pack"). The check runs in the web
  runtime (window.__slothfulStickers): only for downloaded zips up to
  15 MiB, only once the message scrolls into view, one zip at a time,
  cached. Other zips keep the plain file tile, and "Import as Sticker
  Pack" in the message menu covers bigger ones.
- Backup export says that sticker packs only come back in this app when a
  backup is imported elsewhere, shown only to users who have packs.
- Public Bots dialog takes an initialQuery; the community-suggestions
  setting description names the sticker link too.
